@{
   ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
   ExpenseWise helps groups keep shared expense and repayment records. This page describes information handled by the
   application. Each ExpenseWise service is managed by the person or organization operating it. If someone else
   operates the service you use, contact them about their privacy practices.
</p>

<h2>Information stored</h2>
<p>ExpenseWise stores information needed to provide its account and group ledger features, including:</p>
<ul>
   <li>
      Account details such as your name, email address, phone number, and country code. Email is used to sign in;
      phone number and country code are used when a group organizer adds an existing user to a group.
   </li>
   <li>
      Your password is used to protect your account and is not stored in readable form.
   </li>
   <li>
      Group details such as the group name, optional start and end dates, organizer, and members.
   </li>
   <li>
      Expense and repayment records. These include expense descriptions and amounts, payers, people who recorded
      expenses, participant shares, repayment amounts, senders and recipients, and when repayments were recorded.
   </li>
</ul>

<h2>How information is used and shared</h2>
<p>
   The application uses account information to let users sign in, and group and ledger information to show group
   activity and calculate balances. Members of a group can see that group's members, expenses, shares, balances, and
   repayment history. Group organizers can add existing users and record expenses and repayments. Adding a member
   does not send an invitation message.
</p>
<p>
   ExpenseWise is a ledger, not a payment service. It does not move or verify money. Repayment entries are records
   entered in the application; any actual transfer happens outside ExpenseWise. The application does not send email
   or text-message notifications.
</p>

<h2>Storage and service providers</h2>
<p>
   Account and ledger information is kept by the operator of the ExpenseWise service you use. The application also
   uses necessary sign-in information to keep you signed in.
</p>
<p>
   The operator may use service providers to host, maintain, or monitor the service. Those providers may process
   information as part of providing their services. Contact the operator to learn which providers are involved and how
   their practices apply to your information.
</p>
<p>
   The service may collect information to help keep it operating and address problems. The operator controls who can
   access stored information and copies, as well as how long they are kept. Archiving a group does not delete its
   ledger records. Contact the operator with questions about access to or removal of your data.
</p>